# OmniSearch AI configuration
#
# Every variable below is OPTIONAL. With an empty environment, OmniSearch
# boots on SQLite, generates its own session-signing secret on first run, and
# is fully usable: register, ingest a public GitHub repo / local path / ZIP,
# text search, regex search, browse code. Nothing here is required to start.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Storage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the SQLite database and cloned/extracted repositories live.
# OMNISEARCH_DATA_DIR=.omnisearch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absent: a random secret is generated once and persisted to
# <OMNISEARCH_DATA_DIR>/session-secret (0600 permissions) — fine for local
# use. Set this explicitly for any shared or long-lived deployment so
# sessions survive a data-dir wipe and aren't tied to one machine.
# OMNISEARCH_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ingestion limits
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OMNISEARCH_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=200
# OMNISEARCH_MAX_FILE_SIZE_KB=2048

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limiting (in-memory, per process — fine for a single instance)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OMNISEARCH_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=10
# OMNISEARCH_SEARCH_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=60

# Used for absolute URLs in metadata.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reserved for later phases — not read by any code yet, listed so the shape
# of the eventual configuration is visible. See README → Roadmap.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=          # AI repository Q&A (phase 5)
# DATABASE_URL=                # swap SQLite for Postgres + pgvector (phase 4)
# GITHUB_TOKEN=                # connected/private repositories (phase 6)
